<title>USA: IFC syndicates loan to Argentine oil company.</title>
<headline>IFC syndicates loan to Argentine oil company.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Finance Corp on Monday said it had sucessfully completed a $70 million financing package for Companias Asociadas Petroleras of Argentina to assist in a secondary oil recovery program.</p>
<p>The World Bank affiliate that supports private sector development said the investment will finance a large-scale drilling program in the Diadema oil field, located in Chubut province of Southern Argentina.</p>
<p>IFC will provide a $12 million loan as well as a $5.0 million quasi-equity investment for its own account. The rest will come from a variety of investors.</p>
</text>
